    "Notes Updated": "12/15/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Just has not hit to the level you'd want to see\n Not showing improved power, not showing much hit tool\n Takes a ton of walks and also gets a lot of HBP's\n Not sustainable in MLB unless you also actually hit the ball\n Glove is not very good, he struggles to catch velocity and stuff with big movement.\n Arm improved actually, but still fringe average at best\n Likely org depth at this point. Still love him as a competitor.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/16/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Miller's bat is really interesting for a catcher.\n  Has shown power to the biggest parts of the park.\n  Takes walks and doesn't have a big strikeout issue.\n  Defensively is a really solid receiver.\n  Plays with some fire and appears to lead a pitching staff well.\n  There's one big flaw for Miller... In full season ball over two seasons he has allowed 229 stolen bases and only caught 32 (14% for a CS%). This will likely prevent him from ever being able to catch in the majors.\n  The bat could still be good enough to play first if it keeps developing.\n  Holding out hope that they can turn him into at least a mediocre thrower of the baseball, as I think that would move him into a completely different tier if that happened.\"",
